<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Iraq</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – 1958 CE · capital Baghdad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hashemite monarchy that ruled Iraq from 1921 until the revolution of 1958, balancing British influence, Arab nationalism and a divided society.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-i-of-iraq">Faisal I</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-bin-ali-king-of-hejaz">Sharif Hussein</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and leader of the Arab Revolt, was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in August 1921 under the British mandate. The monarchy gained formal independence when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mandatory-iraq">Mandatory Iraq</a> ended in 1932.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> with a parliament dominated by landowners, tribal sheikhs and ex-Ottoman officers, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> kept bases and influence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-i-of-iraq">Faisal I</a> died in 1933 and was followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> and the boy king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq">Faisal II</a>, under the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-ilah">Abd al-Ilah</a>. The period saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simele-massacre">Simele massacre</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> in 1933, the Arab world's first military coup in 1936, and in 1941 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-ali-al-gaylani">Rashid Ali</a>'s pro-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> coup, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-iraqi-war">Anglo-Iraqi War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farhud">Farhud</a> pogrom against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. Oil revenue funded development, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuri-al-said">Nuri al-Said</a> dominated politics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1955 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact">Baghdad Pact</a>, and in 1958 it formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arab-federation">Arab Federation</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Jordan</a>. On 14 July 1958 army officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> overthrew the monarchy; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq">Faisal II</a> and much of the royal family were killed, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-iraq">Republic of Iraq</a> was proclaimed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-iraq.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Iraq" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iraq_(1924%E2%80%931959).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – 1958 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baghdad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Faisal I, Ghazi, Faisal II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia and Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, Kurdish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hashemite Kingdom of Iraq, Iraq</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1940&amp;focus=kingdom-of-iraq" aria-label="Kingdom of Iraq on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5814 968 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Iraq lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6134 1224L6134 1224